(5263931, 764379, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677020" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award WINNER!<br/>seemingly simple, but not really.  I like it.</td>', 'PostLuminous Award WINNER!seemingly simple, but not really.  I like it.', '2009-02-18 19:25:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263936, 764577, 50641, '<td valign="top">Melethia I worked long and hard on that pan - and I''d bet you are underestimating your own artistic talents again ;-)  Maybe we need a decrepit cookware side-challenge!  p.s. apple head is safe and shrinking away.  Bear I think you will get extra points for WS. CC you hit it on the head - Looks like nosferatu to me tu! For anyone who might doubt it still, Posthumous is indeed an amazing artist.</td>', 'Melethia I worked long and hard on that pan - and I''d bet you are underestimating your own artistic talents again ;-)  Maybe we need a decrepit cookware side-challenge!  p.s. apple head is safe and shrinking away.  Bear I think you will get extra points for WS. CC you hit it on the head - Looks like nosferatu to me tu! For anyone who might doubt it still, Posthumous is indeed an amazing artist.', '2009-02-18 19:32:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5263964, 763087, 20748, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sceneit:</b></div><hr/><i> What would some of you do if you couldn''t<br/>perfect your pics in photoshop.....I know very little about it.<br/>I may only have a few good photos but look at the amount of shop that is used.<br/>Some of the comments here sound like you are angry that the photo isn''t perfected to YOUR standards. The other people took it for what it was and commented in a respectful way. It''s whatever. I like my photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If we didn''t have photoshop, I think we would still take the time to think about focus, exposure, and other distracting elements within the viewfinder. I''m sure if you take a second go at this, it would come out much better. Don''t forget to use the maximum pixels when resizing. I gave you a 6 for originality at least. I don''t think the blue ribbon winner deserved theirs with a complete rip-off execution either...</td>', 'Originally posted by sceneit: What would some of you do if you couldn''tperfect your pics in photoshop.....I know very little about it.I may only have a few good photos but look at the amount of shop that is used.Some of the comments here sound like you are angry that the photo isn''t perfected to YOUR standards. The other people took it for what it was and commented in a respectful way. It''s whatever. I like my photo.   If we didn''t have photoshop, I think we would still take the time to think about focus, exposure, and other distracting elements within the viewfinder. I''m sure if you take a second go at this, it would come out much better. Don''t forget to use the maximum pixels when resizing. I gave you a 6 for originality at least. I don''t think the blue ribbon winner deserved theirs with a complete rip-off execution either...', '2009-02-18 19:51:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5264063, 764579, 87808, '<td valign="top">unbelievable that you got all those votes under 5.  this was my top pick for Blue</td>', 'unbelievable that you got all those votes under 5.  this was my top pick for Blue', '2009-02-18 20:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5264110, 762784, 20956, '<td valign="top">I been a casual observer of this site for a few years now. I have had a tendency to stop voting for the photos on this site because I am usually in total disagreement with the weekly winners. I have had a hard time figuring how my ideas of a winner and the actual winners can differ so much. To me it seems that it is more of contest of who can photoshop better than the photographic skills a person has. And as usual I did not vote this time. But your photo is probably one of the nicest I have seen at DP Challenge. The first thing that strikes me is the warmth that your photo exhibits. The composition is perfect and it''s in focus. I do not know how much processing was involved but it looks it was kept to a minimum. Excellent job, congratulations. The only negative that I could say about your photo is that it did not receive the blue ribbon. Good job.</td>', 'I been a casual observer of this site for a few years now. I have had a tendency to stop voting for the photos on this site because I am usually in total disagreement with the weekly winners. I have had a hard time figuring how my ideas of a winner and the actual winners can differ so much. To me it seems that it is more of contest of who can photoshop better than the photographic skills a person has. And as usual I did not vote this time. But your photo is probably one of the nicest I have seen at DP Challenge. The first thing that strikes me is the warmth that your photo exhibits. The composition is perfect and it''s in focus. I do not know how much processing was involved but it looks it was kept to a minimum. Excellent job, congratulations. The only negative that I could say about your photo is that it did not receive the blue ribbon. Good job.', '2009-02-18 21:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5264249, 762784, 100064, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jccminty:</b></div><hr/><i> I been a casual observer of this site for a few years now. I have had a tendency to stop voting for the photos on this site because I am usually in total disagreement with the weekly winners. I have had a hard time figuring how my ideas of a winner and the actual winners can differ so much. To me it seems that it is more of contest of who can photoshop better than the photographic skills a person has. And as usual I did not vote this time. But your photo is probably one of the nicest I have seen at DP Challenge. The first thing that strikes me is the warmth that your photo exhibits. The composition is perfect and it''s in focus. I do not know how much processing was involved but it looks it was kept to a minimum. Excellent job, congratulations. The only negative that I could say about your photo is that it did not receive the blue ribbon. Good job. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>WOW. Thank you so much! That is a big compliment to me when you see all of the talent here. <br/> <br/>This is my original. The only thing done to put it here was rotated and resized.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=766598" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100064/120/766598.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100064/120/766598.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100064/120/766598.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>The editing steps werent much:<br/> <br/>rotated left<br/> <br/>crop<br/> <br/>sharpen<br/> <br/>brightness/contrast<br/> <br/>border<br/> <br/>resize<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-18 23:51:38.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by jccminty: I been a casual observer of this site for a few years now. I have had a tendency to stop voting for the photos on this site because I am usually in total disagreement with the weekly winners. I have had a hard time figuring how my ideas of a winner and the actual winners can differ so much. To me it seems that it is more of contest of who can photoshop better than the photographic skills a person has. And as usual I did not vote this time. But your photo is probably one of the nicest I have seen at DP Challenge. The first thing that strikes me is the warmth that your photo exhibits. The composition is perfect and it''s in focus. I do not know how much processing was involved but it looks it was kept to a minimum. Excellent job, congratulations. The only negative that I could say about your photo is that it did not receive the blue ribbon. Good job.   WOW. Thank you so much! That is a big compliment to me when you see all of the talent here.  This is my original. The only thing done to put it here was rotated and resized.   The editing steps werent much: rotated left crop sharpen brightness/contrast border resize', '2009-02-18 23:49:39.000000', '2009-02-18 23:51:38.000000', 0),
