(5270968, 763956, 32997, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by C_Steve_G:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent! But NYC is only figuratively an apple... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t get the word "But"...is the suggestion that a figurative apple is less than a literal one?<br/>Perhaps one should ask if photographing an apple in some manner other than being eaten is true to its relationship to people...<br/>I like the way you approached this challenge, and a score is a score such a bore...<br/>The inclusion of the woman in the foreground brings energy to your shot, the lamp framing the building is a perfect little touch...</td>', 'Originally posted by C_Steve_G: Excellent! But NYC is only figuratively an apple...   I don''t get the word "But"...is the suggestion that a figurative apple is less than a literal one?Perhaps one should ask if photographing an apple in some manner other than being eaten is true to its relationship to people...I like the way you approached this challenge, and a score is a score such a bore...The inclusion of the woman in the foreground brings energy to your shot, the lamp framing the building is a perfect little touch...', '2009-02-23 16:22:45.000000', NULL, 0),
